"Diagnosis: the E2E hang was NOT map generation. new_player (server/src/ecs_extension.rs:80) hard-requires a named entity 'allegiance1' (from_name(\"allegiance1\")); the test mapPack did not seed the allegiance entities, so new_player returned Err during identity_connected and the client connect hung (no onConnect/onConnectError). Map generation was never reached. Real remaining hardening for minimal themes: weighted_sampler::sample (server/src/asset/weighted_sampler.rs:34) panics 'Invalid weighted selection.' when a selector is empty (total_weight 0), and generate_path_layout indexes room_handles by main_room_count/main_room_count-1 which would panic if fewer rooms were produced. Plan: (1) make weighted_sampler.sample return Option and make generate_path_layout robust to empty selectors / few rooms (no panics); add rust unit tests. (2) Add an E2E map-generation phase with a test AssetPack that includes allegiance1/allegiance2 + a minimal theme + a tiny fixed-seed map, asserting the generated room/path graph. Also worth a separate task: new_player should not hard-depend on a magic 'allegiance1' name."